# Which studio this build talks to.
#
# Exactly one EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL may be uncommented — the last one wins, which
# is a confusing way to find out you edited the wrong line. Swap by moving the
# `#`, then RESTART METRO: EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined at bundle time, not read at
# runtime, so without a restart the old URL stays baked into the bundle.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and uncomment the one you want. Nothing is active here
# on purpose: a fresh clone should not write to production because it forgot to
# read this file.

# ── Production ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deployed studio. Real accounts, real emails through Resend, real rows.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://spoofkitchen.com

# ── Local, from the iOS simulator ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The simulator shares the Mac's network, so localhost is the Mac.
# Needs `npm run dev` in ~/Documents/web_projects/content_kitchen.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Local, from a real phone ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A phone's localhost is the PHONE, so it needs the Mac's LAN address. Next
# binds to localhost by default and will not answer from another device —
# start it as `next dev -H 0.0.0.0`. Replace the address with your own.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.0.10:3000

# ── Unset ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comment out every line above and src/api/config.ts derives the host Metro is
# served from and assumes port 3000 — which is the right answer on both a
# simulator and a phone, as long as the studio is running and reachable.
